  "decision": "FAIL / NO_CANDIDATE_ADMITTED / NO_ROBUST_FACTOR_PASS. F-BDLEV-ANNUAL-US used first-release Federal Reserve Z.1 Security Brokers and Dealers balance sheets and same-release four-quarter book-leverage growth to avoid revision leakage. It produced CAGR 14.210130%, Sharpe 1.487671 and MDD 8.627785%, underperforming frozen V11 on CAGR and Sharpe and underperforming its availability-matched unconditional retention control (CAGR 14.377894%, Sharpe 1.495851). Although candidate Sharpe was at least matched-control Sharpe in 5/7 fixed folds, full-history evidence was adverse. Paired 63-session moving-block bootstrap over 20,000 replicates gave P(CAGR candidate > V11)=24.465% and P(Sharpe candidate > matched)=21.715%; both median incremental deltas were negative. Candidate MDD P97.5=14.697% passed the 15% risk ceiling, but cumulative 28-trial DSR probability was only 91.737%, below 95%. Per the frozen stop rule, no quarterly-change, level, sign reversal, capital-ratio, winsorization, alternate horizon, retention, release-lag, stale-window or ensemble rescue is permitted in this campaign.",
